\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Research waves at ICLR: share of discovery submissions listing each author keyword, 2018--2026; dots mark the peak. The eight keywords were chosen for display after their curves were known. Across the 68 most frequent keywords, 17 peaked in 2019--2024 with shares of at most half the peak both before it and in 2026. Uses no acceptance data.}}{2}{figure.caption.17}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces (a) Emerging (bars) and declining (grey diamonds) topics on $k = 100$ maps fitted on different years, same 43,480 papers; right-hand labels: emerging count (share of 2024--2026 papers in emerging topics, 22.3\% on the 2017--2020 map against 40.9\% on the all-years map). All years (refit): the all-years map refitted with another seed. Topic size `predicts' two-year growth only on the all-years map ($R^2$ 0.28 against $-$0.03; no paired test). (b) Share of submissions building on an FM (blue circles) and proposing a new architecture (orange squares); LLM labels. Inset: the registered test of the package shift, \textsc {replicated} (held-out confirms direction, not size). Uses no acceptance data.}}{9}{figure.caption.34}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Entry contrasts within topic and year (pp) with 95\% intervals: discovery (blue circles) and held-out (orange squares). Rows 1--2, newcomer minus incumbent papers, are registered and \textsc {replicated} (held-out confirms direction, not size). Rows 3--5 are \textsc {exploratory} (discovery only): row 3 compares papers by topic newcomers with an ICLR record with incumbent papers (first-time teams controlled separately; class, FM and team-size controls); row 4 compares first-time teams with returning topic newcomers, and row 5 with all teams that have an ICLR record. Grey: the side the herding prediction expected. Uses no acceptance data.}}{12}{figure.caption.40}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Gate tests by reference point: discovery estimates (blue circles) and held-out declared tests (orange squares), 95\% intervals; the held-out verdict is at right (supported: \textsc {held-out supported}; uninformative: not supported and below the test's MDE80; not supported: a declared test without a registered MDE80). Each row has its own scale: pp for the far jump, insider, branded title and least-distant fifth; pp per log unit for crowding; per 0.1 cosine and per 10 percentile points for the two same-author slopes. Compare replication status, not size. Crowding was registered; title style had been explored before registration; the other rows were found post hoc in discovery. Each held-out test was declared before any held-out estimate for that question was computed.}}{17}{figure.caption.49}%
